---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="alert-notify Documentation: Svelte"
  description="Use alert-notify in Svelte 5 with optional Toaster.svelte, Svelte-aware toast icons, and custom() for components."
  pageTitle="Svelte"
>
  <p>
    <span class="tier helper">Helper</span>
    Svelte ships <code>Toaster.svelte</code> plus <code>toast</code> / <code>custom</code> from
    <code>alert-notify/svelte/toast</code>.
    For a live demo and install snippet, see the <a href="/svelte">Svelte landing</a>.
  </p>

  <pre class="api"><code>{`<script>
  import Toaster from "alert-notify/svelte";
  import { toast, custom } from "alert-notify/svelte/toast";
  import Icon from "./Icon.svelte";
</script>

<Toaster position="top-right" richColors />
<button onclick={() => toast.success("Saved")}>Save</button>
<button
  onclick={() =>
    toast.info("Pay with card", {
      icon: { component: Icon, props: { name: "card" } },
    })
  }
>
  With icon
</button>`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Custom Svelte content</h2>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`import { custom } from "alert-notify/svelte/toast";
import Panel from "./Panel.svelte";

custom({ component: Panel, props: { title: "Hello" } }, { autoClose: false });`}</code></pre>

  <ul class="notes">
    <li>Peer dependency: svelte &gt;= 5.</li>
    <li>Keep using core <code>toast.custom(el)</code> for plain DOM nodes.</li>
    <li>Landing page: <a href="/svelte">/svelte</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
